3. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

   This software depends on third-party components licensed separately by their
   respective owners, including but not limited to OpenCV (Apache-2.0), NumPy,
   SciPy, GDAL (MIT/X), PostgreSQL, PostGIS (GPL-2.0-or-later), FastAPI,
   SQLAlchemy, Celery, React, and PyTorch. Their licences govern those
   components and are not superseded by this file.

   ★ POSTGIS IS GPL-2.0-or-later. LandExplorer communicates with PostgreSQL/
     PostGIS over a network protocol and does not link against, embed, or derive
     from it, so PostGIS's terms do not extend to this software. Do not change
     that arrangement without legal review.

4. MODEL WEIGHTS ARE NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENCE

   ★ THIS SECTION EXISTS BECAUSE IT IS THE MOST LIKELY WAY TO BREACH A LICENCE
     WITH THIS SOFTWARE.

   No model weight files are distributed with this software. Weights fetched via
   `scripts/download_models.py` are licensed by their respective publishers, and
   those licences are frequently NOT open-source licences and NOT compatible
   with commercial use.

   Specifically, and non-exhaustively:

     · SuperPoint (Magic Leap)  — RESEARCH / NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY
     · SuperGlue  (Magic Leap)  — RESEARCH / NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY
     · LightGlue  (ETH Zurich)  — Apache-2.0
     · DINOv2     (Meta)        — Apache-2.0
     · SAM        (Meta)        — Apache-2.0

   A ground control point is a survey coordinate that a client may build on,
   file against, or litigate over. Producing one commercially with a
   non-commercial weight file is a licence violation by the operator. The
   downloader prints each licence and refuses to fetch without an explicit
   acknowledgement.

   (In the current build the deep model backends are DEFERRED and no code path
   loads a weight file at all — see docs/architecture/SCOPE.md. This clause
   governs the moment that changes.)

5. IMAGERY IS NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENCE

   Satellite and aerial imagery retrieved through this software is licensed by
   its provider, not by the copyright holder. Attribution obligations, caching
   limits, and restrictions on derived products are the OPERATOR'S
   responsibility. See docs/legal/imagery-terms.md and README.md.

   Google Earth imagery is not accessible through this software and must not be
   made so.

